A||||0||JIM GOOSE||KONI STRUTS.....problem||||3||
Z||000000||JIM GOOSE||09-17-1999||09:47 AM||||Recently set out to replace struts & shox on my 88 gt.  Tried MONROES and car felt floaty and even squirrely at times. Finally couldnt stand it & bgt KONI struts, everything went OK until tried to inst. on rt. side. The upper bolt wouldnt go thru the hole in the knuckle due to being misaligned. Discovered this was due to interference of knuckle with strut body. Comparing to stock part, the KONI has 1/16" less clearance in this area because stock strut has cutout much larger. Also the knuckle on the rt. side measured 1/16" thicker than left side, took my angle grinder & ground this off. VOILA!! it fits now!! Wouldn't have had the problem if KONI put the cutout in their strut just like stock item & of course, much extra work and gritting my teeth!!!||||reg||3
